<PARA INFOID = "T010254A133" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "15Dec2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Piston</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The pistons have been made lighter by optimizing the cast-out area above the outside of the pin bosses and the skirt shape. In addition, the area of the piston skirt has been reduced (asymmetrical left and right), and a striated finish and resin coating with excellent seizure resistance have been applied, reducing noise and friction.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A tapered squish combustion chamber is provided on the piston top to achieve stable combustion, and together with the pentroof type combustion chamber on the cylinder head side, a high compression ratio has been achieved, providing both high performance and low fuel consumption. In addition, oil jet cooling has been adopted to reduce piston temperature.<XREF     REFID = "S478010257A407"/>
</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Friction has been reduced by making each piston ring thinner and lowering its tension.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Wear resistance has been ensured by applying an alumite treatment<HINTREF REFID = "H478010254A13301"/> to the top ring groove.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<HINT>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT ID = "H478010254A13301">Alumite treatment: A process that electrochemically thickens the oxide film formed when aluminum oxidizes. This oxide film is chemically stable and relatively hard, so it is applied to improve wear resistance.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></HINT>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a3810034p" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "1.806in" />
</FIGURE>
